I have my ticket.
But I still have to stamp the ticket.
I am on the platform now.
I go directly to a pillar.
A small box is hanging there.
The box is yellow.
One must always stamp a paper ticket here.
That is very important.
Without a stamp, the ticket is not valid.
Then a trip with the U-Bahn is expensive.
I push my ticket into the slot.
I hear a loud click.
The box prints a stamp onto the paper.
Now my ticket is valid.
I pack the ticket into my backpack.
I must get in soon.
I wait for the train.
